          "a": "The skunk is a statutory rabies-vector species in Delaware under Title 3, section 8202, and it is handled that way on every job — no bare-hand contact, and pets with any contact go to a veterinarian. Skunk work is done under our Division company permit with certified operators, and any live release happens only when permit conditions allow, in suitable habitat with the landowner's permission and never inside city limits or a state park or wildlife area."
