          "a": "There is nothing to refer out in Rhode Island: DEM's own fact sheet states that no native Rhode Island snake is venomous, timber rattlesnakes disappeared from the state roughly fifty years ago, and copperheads have never been documented here. Snakes are on the NWCS authorized-species list, so our work is identification, hand capture, and release nearby on site — and we will never sell a Rhode Island homeowner protection from a venomous snake that does not live in this state."
