      "leadParagraph": "<p>Striped skunks are statewide in North Carolina, denning under decks, porches, and sheds, and they are a genuine rabies-vector species — second only to raccoons in the state's positive tests.</p>",
      "extendedBody": "<h2>Rules in North Carolina</h2><p>Relocating a trapped skunk is prohibited under 15A NCAC 10B .0106; the lawful outcomes are on-site release after exclusion or humane euthanasia by a licensed WCA. Our crew works den sites with one-way exits where young are not present, then seals the void with buried barriers so the next skunk cannot re-dig it.</p><h2>What the job includes</h2><ul class=\"wildlife-list\"><li><strong>Inspection</strong> — den location and young check.</li><li><strong>Removal</strong> — exclusion-first WCA handling.</li><li><strong>Exclusion</strong> — buried barriers at decks and porches.</li></ul>",
