      "heroSub": "Our crew handles opossum problems across North Carolina — inspection first, lawful removal under NC Wildlife Resources Commission rules, and sealing as one job. Every operator we send is a licensed Wildlife Control Agent (WCA) licensed by the NC Wildlife Resources Commission.",
      "leadParagraph": "<p>Virginia opossums are statewide in North Carolina, sheltering in crawlspaces, under decks, and occasionally in attics, and they are standard licensed WCA depredation work.</p>",
      "extendedBody": "<h2>How we work</h2><p>Our crew removes opossums, checks for young in the pouch season, and seals the crawlspace or deck void that sheltered them — sealing is what keeps the next animal out. We do not use rabies scare copy on opossum pages: opossums are poor rabies candidates and no North Carolina source lists them as a vector of concern.</p><h2>What the job includes</h2><ul class=\"wildlife-list\"><li><strong>Inspection</strong> — shelter site and entry points.</li><li><strong>Removal</strong> — WCA handling under a depredation permit.</li><li><strong>Exclusion</strong> — crawlspace and deck sealing.</li></ul>",
